  "decision": "not adopted. floor-0 regresses real-eval 3.5 pts and collapses idle F1 to ~0.20 on 4/5 seeds; floor-0.5 ties plain MLP on accuracy but idle still collapses on 1/5 seeds (sd 0.23 vs plain MLP 0.013) and confidence separation is slightly worse. No gain for more code + a new hyperparameter. Committed `semlp` candidate = floor 0.5, seed 0 (the best variant, for the record).",
  "finding": "third independent confirmation (after Track B body_raw_hands_derived) that the idle class is fragile to anything reducing feature information \u2014 it needs the full vector to rule gestures out. The SE gate itself is interpretable and validates the feature-block design (suppresses the off-hand for one-hand gestures, leans on the joint-angle block for postures)."
